onal third level also applies when a failed multi-field shard atomically discards otherwise potentially valid companion fields: recover only the unavailable fields using the minimum fresh field-disjoint shards, one attempt each, no retries, and no fourth level.\n\nExact deterministic correction of stale SEO, summaries, sitemaps, calibration analyses, tests, control labels, compatibility write-boundary classifications, or similar derived files is authorized. Preserve the original failed artifacts before correcting derived records. Never rerun the score pass, manually change calculated scores, reuse rejected prose, or alter accepted fields.\n\nA controller or server startup failure occurring before any rendering viewport is attempted may be diagnosed and corrected without consuming a viewport attempt; preserve the failure record. Commit or otherwise freeze and correctly inventory the 40 rendering screenshots before compatibility execution, and remove or safely relocate temporary Playwright controller files so pre-existing rendering artifacts are not misclassified as compatibility writes.\n\nFetch before every push, never force-push, and verify local `HEAD`, local `main`, and `origin/main` equality after every push. Close temporary browser sessions and servers, remove or safely relocate temporary artifacts, and retain required hashed audio and rendering evidence.\n\nStop only if:\n\n- the paid-service cap would be exceeded;\n- required source identity or evidence cannot be established;\n- an allowed model or recovery gate remains invalid after its authorized attempts;\n- repository history has diverged and cannot be reconciled safely;\n- or another genuinely substantive blocker requires new authority.\n\nOn completion, report the selected debates, final scores, paid and direct costs, recovery use, rendering and repository-validation results, production changes, final commit, local/remote equality, and cleanup status. Stop before selecting Batch 17.",
